13 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083394 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "f20159e8-8f86-5bf8-b87e-3eb990b819f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083451 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083451 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084379 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083451 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083451 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083451 #edb/ref 1045 "Calculating Velocity Using Integration" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083451 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186084378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083451 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083451 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "df562fd2-75a6-537c-95d0-fc56957ff191" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084378 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084379 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084378 #edb/ref 1061 617656 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084378 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "100f62e7-30d3-53a3-8066-4c5757c6b8fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084378 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186084389 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084379 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084379 #edb/ref 1061 617657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084379 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "43253f98-3564-58be-b53d-0b7c73ec32e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084379 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083393 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084380 #edb/ref 1061 617660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084380 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "95e07377-0421-53ad-88e4-ea49c586cba0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084380 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083394 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084389 #edb/ref 1064 "For a particle moving along a straight line with velocity $v(t),$ we calculate the acceleration $a(t)$ by differentiating $v$ with respect to $t.$ But what if we're given the acceleration and want to find the velocity?\n\nWe need to do the reverse operation of differentiation, which is int